# Nothing under bin/ is tracked. It is scratch: what `make` dropped there, and
# whatever prebuilt device sim someone fetched to try out. Installed data lives
# with what uses it (src/sty33/sounds for the Teletype recordings) or under
# install/fedora/conf (config this project writes) - never in bin/, which is how
# the Teletype sounds ended up shipping only in the blob tarball. The device
# sims themselves (cbridge, tv11, tvcon, imlac, vt05/50/52, dp3300, dm2500,
# gecon, tek4010, supdup, gw, mlftp, shutdown, mkpty33) are separate programs
# with their own upstreams; see packaging/README.md. Anything deleted from here
# is recoverable from the last commit that had it, and the two engines from
# further back:
#     git checkout <commit> -- bin/<name>
#     git checkout 569c61a^ -- src/panama5     # pidp10.panama's sources
#     git show 1e81df0^:bin/pidp10             # the panama5-era engine
/bin/
build/
# RPM staging and products of make rpm / packaging/build-rpm.sh: dist/ holds
# the Source0/1, dist-rpm/ nothing but RPMs.
# Ignored because --worktree packages `git ls-files --others
# --exclude-standard`: an unignored products dir would put a previous build's
# RPMs inside the tarball of the next one. The directories are overridable
# (DIST_DIR/RPM_DIR), so the names are defaults, not guarantees.
/dist/
/dist-rpm/
# Console-session state an engine run writes into the cwd (a machine-local
# session UUID). Runtime droppings like build/, never package, never commit.
sess
